  "id": "DrugBank_DB11160 - MONDO_6004",
  "verbalization": "Phenyltoloxamine, through its indication for Urticaria and Angioedema, is linked to Rupatadine, which in turn is associated with Vasomotor Rhinitis. This suggests a potential pathway where Phenyltoloxamine may influence the development of Vasomotor Rhinitis via the intermediate of Rupatadine. The evidence is supported by multiple paths, each linking Phenyltoloxamine to a disease that then connects to Rupatadine and finally to Vasomotor Rhinitis. The recurring mechanism involves the use of Rupatadine as a mediator, highlighting a possible role in the pathophysiology of Vasomotor Rhinitis. The integration of these paths supports the hypothesis that Phenyltoloxamine may contribute to Vasomotor Rhinitis through a mechanism involving Rupatadine, though further studies are needed to confirm the direct relationship.",
